// fn run() { (-7).div_euclid(0) }
// expect-stdout numeric-euclid-zero-stop: ""
// expect-exit numeric-euclid-zero-stop: 70
// expect-stderr numeric-euclid-zero-stop: "Stop [E3010]: `divided by zero`\n  --> fixture.jet:1\n Why: The operands or position do not produce a valid result, so the safe runtime stops instead of returning corrupted data — with Jet file and line.\n Fix: Check the operands or bounds before the operation, or use a checked operation that returns an outcome.\nMore: jet-lang.dev/e/E3010\n"
